#: ../../../reference/interfaces/spi-interface.md:2
msgid "spi interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/spi-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"`spi` allows access to a specific Serial Peripheral Interface (SPI) "
"controller. This snap interface is restricted because it provides privileged "
"access to SPI hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/spi-interface.md:8
msgid "**Auto-Connect**: no</br> **Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/spi-interface.md:8
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/spi-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"`path` (slot): path to the specific SPI device node e.g. `/dev/spidev0.0`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/spi-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"Snaps that want to consume an SPI device simply use `plugs: [ spi ]`. The "
"SPI device to connect to is specified during the interface connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/spi-interface.md:14
msgid ""
"To see which SPI slots are available on your system, run `snap connections --"
"all` to show all the possible slots on your system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/spi-interface.md:16
msgid ""
"$ snap connections --all | grep spi\n"
"spi         -        pi:spidev0              -\n"
"spi         -        pi:spidev1              -\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/spi-interface.md:22
msgid ""
"Once connected, the consuming snap can use the device via the path specified "
"by the connected slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/spi-interface.md:24
msgid "Requires snapd version _2.28+_."
msgstr ""
